# b00t Guard Violations datum
# .tomllmd — mdtable format for column-stable serialization
# schema: 1 | bump ONLY on field definition changes
# last_updated: 2026-05-04
#
# 🤓 Documents the guard-violations.jsonl persistence format used by
#    GuardViolationCounter and the `b00t guard violations list` CLI command.
#    File is append-only JSONL — each line is one JSON object.
#    Path: ~/.b00t/guard-violations.jsonl
#
# 🔗参 b00t-cli/src/hive.rs — GuardViolationCounter (load, increment, save)
# 🔗参 b00t-cli/src/commands/guard.rs — `b00t guard violations list` CLI
# 🔗参 _b00t_/hive-guards.hive.toml — guard definitions with repeat_threshold

[b00t]
name = "GUARD-VIOLATIONS"
type = "schema"
hint = "Guard violations persistence format — JSONL schema for guard-violations.jsonl; used by GuardViolationCounter and guard CLI"

[b00t.version]
schema = 1
content = "stable"

## Guard Violation Record Fields
## schema_version=1: these 3 fields in this order.
## Each line in guard-violations.jsonl is a JSON object with these keys.
## Append-mode only — never overwrite the file.

| field | type | description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| pattern | string | Guard pattern that matched (e.g. "pip install", or Rhai expr name) |
| count | u32 | Running violation count for this pattern since last reset |
| last_violation | string | ISO 8601 timestamp of most recent violation (e.g. "2026-05-04T05:30:00Z") |

## Example record
## {
##     "pattern": "pip install",
##     "count": 3,
##     "last_violation": "2026-05-04T05:30:00Z"
## }

## Escalation Logic
## schema_version=1: these 4 columns in this order.
## The GuardViolationCounter implements the 🦨 → 💩 escalation pattern.

| threshold | hit_count | emoji | action |
|-----------|-----------|-------|--------|
| repeat_threshold=None | any | 🦨 | Always warn (no escalation) |
| repeat_threshold=N | count <= N | 🦨 | Warn + redirect |
| repeat_threshold=N | count > N | 💩 | Block + escalate to operator |

## File format notes
##
## - Path: ~/.b00t/guard-violations.jsonl
## - Created on first violation if file doesn't exist
## - Parent directory (~/.b00t/) created automatically
## - OpenOptions::append() — never truncates, never rewrites entire file
## - Loaded on each GuardViolationCounter::load() call via read_to_string + line-by-line parse
## - Reset via GuardViolationCounter::reset_key() — rewrites file excluding the reset pattern
## - Race condition: no locking — single-threaded CLI usage only

